          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::61d22ff9d5992d0ca77a2697",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "material_status"
          ],
          "value": "resolved",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::20fd16b3f23123515d2ab1cc",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "approach"
          ],
          "value": "The authors conducted a systematic review following PRISMA guidelines. They searched PubMed and Cochrane databases for peer-reviewed articles published between December 2015 and December 2024. Inclusion criteria covered randomized/non-randomized clinical trials in humans and animal models investigating the association between microbiome and TNBC treatment response. Data extraction focused on study design, population, interventions, and key findings. Risk of bias was assessed using ROBINS-I, ROB 2, and SYRCLE tools depending on study type. The results were narratively synthesized by grouping studies into human clinical/translational cohorts and murine/preclinical mechanistic models.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::8f171e01ed287c390ec491ca",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "contribution_and_limits"
          ],
          "value": {
            "contribution": "Provides a comprehensive narrative synthesis of both clinical and preclinical evidence linking microbiome features (diversity, specific taxa, metabolites) to TNBC treatment outcomes (pCR, PFS, OS).",
            "limits": "Narrative synthesis only; no meta-analysis performed. Included studies vary widely in design, sample size, and sequencing methods. Many clinical studies have small sample sizes or are retrospective. Causal mechanisms are largely inferred from preclinical data or correlative clinical observations."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::72245b24bdfc15d044586d3d",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Neoadjuvant Chemotherapy (NACT) in early-stage TNBC",
            "finding": "Higher baseline gut microbiome alpha-diversity (Shannon index) is significantly associated with achieving pCR (Vernaci et al., 2023). Specific taxa like Bacteroides eggerthii were enriched in responders."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::304c47cb87333d1dc062c6e4",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Chemoimmunotherapy (Atezolizumab + Chemo) in metastatic TNBC",
            "finding": "High baseline Faith's phylogenetic diversity (PD) predicts prolonged progression-free survival (PFS), particularly in the atezolizumab arm (ALICE trial). Bifidobacterium enrichment was associated with lack of clinical benefit in this specific context."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::6db66cc17b20c3908b19f74b",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Antimicrobial exposure during/after diagnosis",
            "finding": "Cumulative antimicrobial exposure is associated with decreased overall survival (OS) and breast cancer-specific survival (BCS), independent of stage and ANC. This effect persists for up to 3 years post-diagnosis."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::a9d3317ffe930c9f61ed4b00",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Intratumoral Microbiota Load",
            "finding": "Higher intratumoral bacterial burden correlates with pCR to neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy. High load is associated with increased FOLR2+ macrophages and decreased SPP1+ (immunosuppressive) macrophages."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::6e14c2b8fa20304048c48080",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Preclinical Models (Murine)",
            "finding": "Gut microbiota depletion (antibiotics/germ-free) attenuates doxorubicin efficacy and CD8+ T cell infiltration; fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) restores response. Engineered E. coli producing methioninase reduces tumor growth via methionine depletion. Microbial metabolite TMAO promotes anti-PD-1 efficacy via GSDME-mediated pyroptosis."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::359f788dd049bca472959d3e",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "paper_kind"
          ],
          "value": "review",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::4c9f0a7f34e9c68afee2de13",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ],
          "value": "Does the microbiome influence pathological response and clinical outcomes in TNBC patients undergoing standard systemic therapies (chemotherapy and immunotherapy)?",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::511e006a092c44a9c419d77c",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ],
          "value": "Triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC); gut and tumor-associated microbiome; neoadjuvant chemotherapy (NACT) and immune checkpoint blockade (ICB).",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::a0a4c7233ac1d8bc06c65120",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ],
          "value": "This systematic review synthesizes evidence from 14 studies (clinical trials, observational cohorts, and preclinical models) to evaluate the role of the microbiome in TNBC therapeutic response. It specifically investigates whether baseline microbiome composition and diversity predict pathological complete response (pCR) or survival outcomes under NACT and ICB regimens. The review highlights that higher microbial diversity and specific commensal taxa are associated with enhanced antitumor immunity and better treatment efficacy, while antibiotic-induced dysbiosis correlates with poorer outcomes. It also discusses potential mechanisms involving immune cell infiltration, macrophage polarization, and microbial metabolites.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::642caa8ee29d86ce26dbb5ae",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "TNBC lacks ER/PR/HER2 targets, relying on chemo and increasingly ICB. pCR is a key prognostic marker. Antibiotic use is common and linked to poor outcomes."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::0e24f009d6feeb68363b932c",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Antimicrobial exposure is associated with decreased OS/BCS, potentially mediated by lymphopenia and loss of beneficial taxa."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::e6dd32bf5adfccfafd70bce7",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Figure 6 and discussion suggest Chemo alone may destroy diversity, while Chemo+ICB preserves/restores it, allowing beneficial bacteria to reinforce efficacy."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::95484221107528a95136a64f",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "These are observational/correlational findings in humans. The ALICE trial analysis is exploratory. Sample sizes are modest. Does not prove causality for all taxa mentioned.",
            "contribution": "Identifies clinical associations between microbiome features and ICB/Chemo efficacy. Specifically, it reports that high baseline Faith's PD predicts PFS benefit from Atezolizumab+Chemo but not Chemo alone. It also notes that intratumoral microbiota load predicts pCR to NACI.",
            "facet_id": "F1"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::3e9f231228531d8f8721dc30",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "Mechanisms are primarily derived from murine models or in vitro systems. Translational relevance to humans needs careful framing (e.g., TMAO mechanism validated in mice, correlated in small human cohort). Antibiotic depletion models may not fully replicate human dysbiosis.",
            "contribution": "Details mechanistic pathways from preclinical studies: 1) TMAO promotes anti-PD-1 efficacy via GSDME-mediated pyroptosis and CD8+ T cell activation. 2) Gut microbiota depletion reduces Doxorubicin efficacy by impairing CD8+ T cell infiltration and IFN-gamma signaling. 3) Engineered E. coli reduces tumor growth via methionine depletion. 4) Quercetin enhances Cyclophosphamide efficacy via SCFA production and immune modulation.",
            "facet_id": "F2"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::ad46602408c995988ee87e8a",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "The review includes both gut and intratumoral microbiome data; ensure distinction when applying findings to specific anatomical sites.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::a5ae9796ea0328296e6cb150",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Many clinical findings are from small cohorts or retrospective analyses; avoid overstating generalizability.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::9b5c6dc3cdfb4fee6c511be8",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Preclinical mechanisms (e.g., TMAO, methionine depletion) are robust in mice but human validation is often limited or correlative.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::b30dd6261ea8656401646806",
          "source_handle": "P0057",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Taxon-specific effects (e.g., Bifidobacterium being beneficial in melanoma but associated with non-response in this TNBC ICB trial) highlight context-dependency.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::be960d4dd42c49b7fc35ff7b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch2",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_002\\2af2f48e7a68a8b8fa9ae892ee0e5e2536f3aee44be4bd76f4e9431182e6f9b9\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0057"
        },
